Tremulous Revamped (Linux x86_64)
=================================

Play: run ./Tremulous.x86_64   (if it does not start, run: chmod +x Tremulous.x86_64)

Requirements
- 64-bit Linux (x86_64) with glibc @REQ@ or newer (Ubuntu 18.10+, Debian 10+,
  Fedora 29+, RHEL/Rocky 8+, Arch, SteamOS). Measured: the game library needs
  glibc @GLIBC@, the Godot engine binary needs glibc @ENGINE_GLIBC@.
- A graphics driver with Vulkan 1.1 or OpenGL 3.3, and an X11 or Wayland session.
- Sound uses Godot's own audio (PulseAudio / PipeWire / ALSA). The FMOD and
  Steam Audio sound of the Windows build is Windows-only.

4K textures (optional): download both tremulous-revamped-hd-textures zips from
the Tremulous-Revamped GitHub release "hd-textures-v1" and unzip them into this
folder, so you get an "hd" folder next to Tremulous.x86_64.

base/ holds the original Tremulous 1.1 content (see base/COPYING, base/CC and
base/README.txt).
Source code: https://github.com/MeepingsCorner/Tremulous-Revamped (this port);
the original Tremulous code it is ported from: https://github.com/darklegion/tremulous-legacy
This Linux build is made from the same source commit as the Windows build, with
the game library built against an old glibc. Build recipe and checksums:
@REPO_NOTE@
